1
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,390
I never dreamed before

2
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:21,230
I'm gonna knock the door

3
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:24,800
into the world of perfect free

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,900
(You ain't no lonely!)

5
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,740
You're gonna say I'm lying

6
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,470
I'm gonna get the chance

7
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:36,040
I thought a chance is far from me

8
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,210
(You ain't no lonely!)

9
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:40,120
I was made to hit in America

10
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:42,980
(I was made to hit in America)

11
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:48,890
I was made to hit in America

12
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:52,560
You are the sun, you are the star

13
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,560
(To me, forever)

14
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:58,270
You are the sun, you are the star

15
00:00:58,270 --> 00:01:01,200
(To me, forever)

16
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:13,950
I was made to hit in America

17
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:16,790
I was made to hit in America

18
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:19,650
(I was made to hit in America)

19
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:22,460
I was made to hit in America

20
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:25,230
(I was made to hit in America)

21
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:32,860
I was made to hit in America

22
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:39,730
Oh well...

23
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:49,280
Stop...

24
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:56,750
Stop!

25
00:02:12,210 --> 00:02:14,580
Koyuki is the best!

26
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,680
Have you lost your mind?

27
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,710
What the hell are you saying
all of a sudden?

28
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:21,650
I said Koyuki is the best.

29
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:24,820
The vocalist for your band's
gotta be Koyuki.

30
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:30,390
He's a genius. He's gonna
be a fucking great vocalist.

31
00:02:30,390 --> 00:02:34,900
Hey, we're not talking about
making the choir here, understand?

32
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:38,000
Now really, you don't understand!

33
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,940
What are they fighting about?
I can't understand them at all.

34
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:44,110
I think Koyuki will be great too!

35
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:45,400
Huh?!

36
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:53,650
The vocalist for the band.
I think Koyuki will be good!

37
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:55,240
Vocalist?

38
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:01,810
Koyuki and Chiba, huh?

39
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:10,660
W-what? What're you looking at?!

40
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:12,680
Yukio! You have a letter from Hiro-kun!

41
00:04:13,950 --> 00:04:16,960
"How are you, Yukio-kun?
I'm doing very well right now."

42
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:20,960
"I won the Kyushu
Piano Contest the other day!"

43
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:23,960
"Do you know how big that is?
I might even go to Vienna!"

44
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:25,930
"P.S. I bought the latest Sangokushi."

45
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:33,210
Let's see...

46
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:36,040
"Dear Hiro-kun,"

47
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:42,880
"Thank you for your letter.
I've started playing the guitar."

48
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:48,060
"It's surprisingly easy to play."

49
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:51,790
"I've mastered music played
by Van Halen, Steve Vai,

50
00:04:51,790 --> 00:05:04,070
Paul Gilbert, Nuno, Zakk Wylde,
and even Yot-chan..."

51
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:08,310
"I'm practicing
'The Song of the Seasons' right now."

52
00:05:08,310 --> 00:05:13,980
"Wouldn't it be great if we
could play together in Vienna?"

53
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:20,790
"The photo I've enclosed was taken
at the East Japan Guitar Awards

54
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:23,990
held at the municipal gymnasium."

55
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:29,200
"It's from when I won in
the middle school division."

56
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:30,820
"Yours truly..."

57
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:38,900
Mom, I'm going to the gymnasium!

58
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:11,670
What am I doing anyway?

59
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:27,250
It's almost summer vacation...

60
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:36,090
All right! First, I'm gonna
find me a giant beetle!

61
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:21,810
Today's cloudy skies
will clear up with time

62
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:27,110
Go for it, don't be tied down,
set yourself free

63
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:33,850
Feel free, yes,
the new tomorrow is wow wow

64
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:41,460
So cheer up,
because I want to see your smile

65
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:01,940
H-hello...

66
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,950
I-I'm sorry!

67
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:15,060
Who was that kid?

68
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,000
Koyuki.

69
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,540
-About time you leave.
-Huh? Forget that kid.

70
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:23,540
Go home!

71
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,940
He's more important than me?

72
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:26,940
Yeah.

73
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:32,970
You felt differently yesterday!
You were so nice yesterday...

74
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,270
You're the pits!

75
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,060
-Yo!
-I-I'm sorry!

76
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:49,330
Granny's not here now.
Let's practice a song.

77
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:51,800
Ryusuke-kun...I...

78
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:54,500
I have to talk to you.

79
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,770
What is it?

80
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,750
Get the fuck outta here!

81
00:09:30,970 --> 00:09:34,130
Never come around again.

82
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:38,880
I'm so sorry!

83
00:09:51,530 --> 00:09:55,460
I'm sorry...I'm sorry...

84
00:09:56,300 --> 00:10:00,630
I'm sorry...I'm sorry!

85
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:02,300
I'm sorry...

86
00:10:44,950 --> 00:10:46,510
All right!

87
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:51,290
First, get the lane markers
and we'll go 200 meters four times!

88
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:54,150
-Are you serious?!
-We'll die!

89
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:56,260
I won't allow any slacking!

90
00:10:56,260 --> 00:11:02,660
This summer, we're gonna get
way better than the rival schools!

91
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:05,930
Umm...What about my plans
as team advisor?

92
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,270
Boy, that interim coach is tough.

93
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:17,210
It's only been two weeks,
but he's way more than interim!

94
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:22,480
If this keeps up, everyone will
quit the team! But he sure is tough!

95
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:28,190
Saito-san is a fanatic who swims
over 30,000 meters every week!

96
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:31,690
It's like, is he really 44?!

97
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:36,000
By the way, isn't Koyuki-kun
joining the team?

98
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,630
He's in a bit of a bind right now.

99
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:43,740
-Bind?
-Yeah.

100
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:46,400
I wonder if he's okay.

101
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:53,080
Hey, you two girls! No slacking!

102
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,710
-Sorry!
-Sorry!

103
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:13,230
Yukio, you have a letter from Hiro-kun!

104
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:18,210
"I'm shocked you started
playing the guitar."

105
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:20,710
"But I bet you're still
no match for my piano skills."

106
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:23,210
"I wanna hear how good you are.
Play for me whenever I visit next."

107
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:26,580
"P.S. I didn't get to go to Vienna,
but I did visit Holland Town."

108
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:57,080
Huh? Koyuki-kun, right?

109
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,580
Yes.

110
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:02,980
Did something happen? I haven't
seen you at the pool since then.

111
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,350
No.

112
00:13:04,350 --> 00:13:06,350
You play the guitar?

113
00:13:06,350 --> 00:13:09,220
Err...no...

114
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:15,500
-This is...
-Oh boy, that's bad!

115
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,900
Yes...

116
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:20,300
Once it's broken...

117
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:24,600
Broken things can't be fixed.

118
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:27,040
-I wonder about that.
-Huh?

119
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:30,440
This guitar can probably be fixed.

120
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:35,380
My friend will do it for cheap.
Give it a month and it'll be fixed.

121
00:13:36,450 --> 00:13:37,940
It can be fixed?

122
00:13:40,550 --> 00:13:42,080
Saito-san...

123
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:48,430
I may not look like it,
but British rock changed my life.

124
00:13:48,430 --> 00:13:50,400
Saito-san...

125
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,670
Poor guitar, if you throw it away.

126
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:57,800
Come on over anytime,
and bring that guitar.

127
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,870
If you'd like, I'd be happy to teach you.

128
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,140
See you!

129
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:15,210
All right.

130
00:14:31,910 --> 00:14:34,510
This is pitiful...

131
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:36,810
About Koyuki...

132
00:14:39,450 --> 00:14:44,180
That guitar was given to me by Eddie.

133
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:46,790
No one would give me the time of day...

134
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:51,590
And it was Eddie who took the time
to talk to this Japanese kid.

135
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:53,650
But even Koyuki...

136
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:58,330
Ryusuke-kun...

137
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:01,100
Hey! Look, look!

138
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,270
Look what I got!

139
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:16,740
-Hey, Ryusuke! Help me!
-Huh?

140
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:22,090
Here you are, Izumi-chan!

141
00:15:22,090 --> 00:15:23,790
Oh, thanks...

142
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:27,160
-Don't mention it!
-Huh? What about for me?

143
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,230
-It was hilarious the other day...
-Huh?
-Huh?

144
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:33,270
Ryusuke's never eaten natto in his life.

145
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:35,940
-Huh?! You serious?!
-So

146
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,900
Hey. It's almost time.

147
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,370
-Right.
-Right.

148
00:15:39,370 --> 00:15:41,310
Man, who cares about the concert?

149
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:45,950
-Don't you want to make
summer memories with me?
-Let's go!

150
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:51,410
Hey! I'm coming, too! C'mon!
It'd be the perfect double date!

151
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,920
Can't think of a band without him.

152
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,910
Yeah, definitely funky.

153
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:48,980
Man, the vocals were terrible!

154
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,110
What the hell-?!

155
00:16:50,110 --> 00:16:55,380
With vocals like that,
I feel sorry for Taira.

156
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:56,720
Why you-!

157
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,720
Good evening, everyone!

158
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:03,420
I'm Manabu and I used to
do vocals with The Crowd!

159
00:17:03,420 --> 00:17:06,930
-Manabu!
-Sing for us!

160
00:17:06,930 --> 00:17:08,560
You're so cool!

161
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,860
Switch with me, you're terrible.

162
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,630
Why you-!

163
00:17:20,010 --> 00:17:22,240
Sing, Manabu!

164
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,110
Ryusuke-kun...

165
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:28,620
I know. This was Eiji's idea.

166
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:32,550
Well, since I'm on stage,
maybe I'll sing.

167
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:35,720
The Music Men are here,

168
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:40,350
so maybe I'll sing "Journey"
by the Heartbreakers!

169
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:46,730
What'll we do?

170
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:48,670
Hurry and sing!

171
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:07,990
Who's calling my name?
I hear the voice of legends

172
00:18:07,990 --> 00:18:14,290
What do I want?
Static emotion comes down

173
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:19,600
Did I have the dream?
Am I misunderstood?

174
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:25,570
What do I want?
Static emotion comes down

175
00:18:25,570 --> 00:18:28,270
-I'm going home.
-What?

176
00:18:28,270 --> 00:18:31,300
I don't know what's good about him at all.

177
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:47,960
"Saito Paper Company"

178
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,630
"Saito Paper Company"

179
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:53,330
That's it! F is played by
pressing down with your index finger.

180
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:56,870
Hmm...pretty good.

181
00:18:56,870 --> 00:18:58,340
Really?

182
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:02,210
You're progressing nicely.
You can make sounds now.

183
00:19:02,210 --> 00:19:04,510
Yeah.

184
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:07,480
Now that you've gotten
the hang of common chords,

185
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:10,420
let's try to play continuously.

186
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,750
Uhh...My fingers...

187
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,890
Hurt, don't they?

188
00:19:14,890 --> 00:19:18,220
But if you give up now,
you won't make it with girls.

189
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:21,230
No, that's not what I-

190
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:23,860
Koyuki-kun. Observe.

191
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,490
T-that's amazing!

192
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:33,570
Koyuki-kun, come with me.

193
00:19:33,570 --> 00:19:35,010
Okay.

194
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:49,520
When I got injured and had
my Olympic dreams shattered,

195
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:53,250
I felt so sorry for myself,
and my only consolation...

196
00:19:59,470 --> 00:20:01,300
...was guitars!

197
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:04,200
Which one do you like, Koyuki-kun?

198
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:11,340
The guitar on the left is
the same shape as Ryusuke-kun's!

199
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:16,280
Oh...I'll bet that one
is a Gibson Les Paul.

200
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:20,290
But mine is a fake
called the Tibson Les Paul.

201
00:20:20,290 --> 00:20:25,250
When it was 360 yen to the dollar,
I couldn't afford the real McCoy.

202
00:20:26,390 --> 00:20:28,430
Tibson?

203
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:31,600
Now then...I'll let you
borrow this Les Paul.

204
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,570
Huh?! Are you sure?!

205
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:38,670
You'll also need a tuning machine,
and...an amp.

206
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:45,040
Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool! Fool!

207
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,110
"My name is Page."

208
00:20:46,110 --> 00:20:47,850
"My name is Page."

209
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:52,120
Ever heard of a band
called the Rocket Boys?

210
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,550
Fool!

211
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:57,860
They're a mystery British group,
overshadowed by the Beatles,

212
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:00,790
who recorded one album
and then broke up.

213
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:03,320
They're the teachers of my soul.

214
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:10,400
Follow me

215
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:15,710
Baby, I won't let you leave
if you believe in me

216
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:18,650
-And I always set you free
from all those yesteryears

217
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:18,650
-A-amazing!

218
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:20,380
-And I always set you free
from all those yesteryears

219
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:20,380
-I've never seen a bird like that,

220
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:22,180
even on TV.

221
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:23,020
That's Page.

222
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:28,550
The one and only friend of Kenichi Saito,
age 44 and unmarried.

223
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:36,130
Fool!

224
00:21:36,130 --> 00:21:39,860
Making him sing is my goal.

225
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:01,220
Dammit!

226
00:22:02,890 --> 00:22:06,380
He'll only respond to great music!

227
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:12,430
Koyuki-kun! Let's do our best
to make Page sing!

228
00:22:12,430 --> 00:22:15,470
All right! If I'm going to try,
I may as well give it my best!

229
00:22:15,470 --> 00:22:17,500
That's the spirit, Koyuki-kun!

230
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:20,770
Just wait! We'll make him sing for us!

231
00:22:20,770 --> 00:22:23,780
Yes! Atta boy, Koyuki-kun!

232
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:27,080
Of the three feudal generals,
I like Nobunaga the best.

233
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:31,580
Fool!

234
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,950
Okay then, let's start today's practice!

235
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:36,220
All right! Please teach me!

236
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:37,860
A!

237
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,530
D!

238
00:22:39,530 --> 00:22:41,060
G!

239
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,550
F!

240
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:52,340
Another minute

241
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:55,280
Feelin' so fine

242
00:22:57,350 --> 00:22:59,580
You turn the freeze

243
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:02,410
into warm light

244
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:07,990
Had a premonition

245
00:23:07,990 --> 00:23:10,690
I've been waitin' ever since

246
00:23:10,690 --> 00:23:14,200
My world comin' down

247
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:16,720
It's got me spinnin' 'round

248
00:23:18,770 --> 00:23:25,110
If you really wanna fly

249
00:23:25,110 --> 00:23:27,870
you gotta let go

250
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:42,290
Simply the most

251
00:23:42,290 --> 00:23:44,330
big sensation

252
00:23:44,330 --> 00:23:47,130
(once you're here you won't go back)

253
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:49,400
She's really pretty

254
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:51,470
One-eyed vision

255
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:54,240
(lose the fear it don't come back)

256
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:57,910
Little sister showed me

257
00:23:57,910 --> 00:24:00,540
Really took me for a ride

258
00:24:00,540 --> 00:24:02,140
My world comin' down

259
00:24:02,140 --> 00:24:05,610
(once you're here you won't go back)

